From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:47:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09074/11362] Close the gaps: REQ-ARC-WMTE-6260 spec entry, and
 re-publish the stale Kaggle code dataset

SPEC GAP. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6260 was in ops/known-issues.md but never in the capability
spec. Added with its result: 0 of 4 non-degenerate predicates; the "gate met"
verdict is a false positive from a gate that required only a sensitivity gain and
never consulted the paired specificity; and the pre-registered consequence that
prompt-level work on the goal predicate is exhausted.

DATASET GAP. The v15 preview A/B reported ImportError on _llama_server_slots,
meaning the Kaggle code dataset ran older code than this repo. Closing it required
fixing two silent defects in the publish path first:

1. The staleness guard was the stale thing. prep_daily_submission.py aborted with
   "adapter fix (MAX_ACTIONS=400) missing -- stale snapshot", but MAX_ACTIONS went
   400 -> 2000 on 2026-08-07 (488eb8cede, operator directive with a measured budget
   sweep) and the guard was never updated. It has aborted EVERY publish since that
   date while blaming the snapshot -- very likely why the dataset drifted months
   behind. It failed in the safe direction, but a guard whose message misdirects
   does not get fixed, so the marker now tells the reader to check the shipped
   value before assuming the snapshot is at fault.

2. The bundle carried 130 inherited .pyc files, including one for
   arc_executable_world_model -- the exact module whose staleness caused the
   ImportError. The overlay excludes __pycache__ from the repo side but nothing
   removed what the downloaded dataset already had, and zip extraction does not
   preserve mtimes reliably, so stale bytecode shadowing fresh source is a real way
   to publish the new module and still run the old one. Now stripped. The first
   strip was silently undone by the import+build smoke regenerating them, so that
   smoke now runs with -B; verified 0 .pyc in the bundle.

Published with all existing guards passing, including the import+build smoke. The
scored path will now run code matching this repo, so the preview A/B's CONFIG
WARNING should clear and its arms will measure the shipped configuration rather
than the hardware. No default changed: the P4 knobs are env-gated and unset. No
submission was made and the live goal-veto threshold is untouched.

A pending test-suite-mutation marker was cleared deliberately after investigation:
it was armed by a concurrent bare `pytest`, its own attributed_to_run was EMPTY,
and the single file it flagged was this commit's authored edit to
prep_daily_submission.py, not test damage.

